The function already does very little work, so there is not much to gain here. The rewrite below keeps the same checks and results, with two small changes:

- It loads the `profile` member into a local variable once, instead of reading it through `this` each time.
- It marks the "no profile" path as unlikely, so the compiler lays out the common path first.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumSubFields(void) const
{
    const auto p = profile;
    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (idx >= p->numFields), 0))
        return 0;
    return p->fields[idx].numSubFields;
}
```